  "permanent_motion": "Slow, constant pulsing of `gta_glow` and `secondary_glow` opacities to indicate active production zones. The ocean background remains static, but a subtle global map drift could be applied if needed for visual interest, though not strictly required here.",
  "fidelity_warnings": "The 'GTA / GAZ NATUREL' text in the image uses a specific condensed sans-serif font (looks like Bebas Neue or similar), while the prompt specifies IBM Plex Mono for plate labels. Will use a clean sans-serif matching the image visual closely for this specific label to maintain fidelity, while keeping the bottom date overlay in a monospaced or tracking-spaced font. The export arc is a Bezier curve; the exact SVG path parameters provided are an estimation to match the visual curve from Senegal to Europe.",
  "remotion_implementation_notes": "Use Mapbox GL JS for the base map with a custom dark theme (ocean #1c3552, land #4a4a4a, borders #ffffff). The dots and labels should be React components positioned absolutely over the Mapbox canvas, using projected coordinates if the map pans, or just fixed coordinates if static. Animate the `stroke-dasharray` of the SVG `<path>` for the `export_arc` to simulate the line drawing over time.",
